---
source: crates/cache-explorer-core/tests/golden.rs
description: "Write-no-allocate under write-back: a store miss goes around the cache and counts as a write-around; the second writes the value memory already holds (case 9)."
---
1.1 | decode | lineSize | - | - | Store 0x0A4: tag 0x01, set 2, offset 4 (word 1).
1.2 | miss | associativity | accesses, stores, misses | - | Set 2 is invalid. Miss.
1.3 | memWrite | allocatePolicy | memory 0xA4, writearounds | - | Write-no-allocate: 7 goes straight to memory at 0x0A4. The cache is unchanged.
2.1 | decode | lineSize | - | - | Store 0x0A8: tag 0x01, set 2, offset 8 (word 2).
2.2 | miss | associativity | accesses, stores, misses | - | Set 2 is invalid. Miss.
2.3 | memWrite | allocatePolicy | writearounds | - | Write-no-allocate: 66 goes straight to memory at 0x0A8. The cache is unchanged.
